*** Add File: FitFlow/README.md
# FitFlow Android

Native Kotlin and Jetpack Compose application for Android 10+.

## Open and build

1. Open this `FitFlow` folder in Android Studio (Ladybug or later).
2. Set the Android SDK location in `local.properties` when Android Studio prompts.
3. Replace `app/src/main/res/drawable/fitflow_logo.xml` with the supplied official Blue Running-Man image before release. Keep the exact file name.
4. Sync Gradle and run on an Android 10+ device.
5. Create an APK: `Build > Build APK(s)`.
6. Create a Play Store AAB: `Build > Generate Signed Bundle / APK > Android App Bundle` and select a release keystore.

## Play Store release

- Set the production AdMob app ID and ad units in `AndroidManifest.xml` and `AdConfig.kt`.
- Publish a hosted privacy-policy URL and update `AppLinks.PRIVACY_URL`.
- Prepare screenshots, feature graphic, and listing copy in `play-store-assets/`.
- Increment `versionCode` and `versionName` in `app/build.gradle.kts` for every upload.

## GitHub

Create an empty GitHub repository, then from this directory run:

```bash
git add FitFlow
git commit -m "Add FitFlow native Android application"
git push -u origin main
```
